    "reading": {
        "body": "AionLabs has shipped six API-only text models since February 2025, none with open weights, so nothing in this family can be self-hosted.\n\nThe pattern is a closed, steadily refreshed line. Releases arrive in pairs, a full model and a Mini, in February 2025, February 2026, July 2026, and September 2026. Five of the six support reasoning. Context windows grew from 32,768 tokens on the first model to 262,144 on the newest two, while the output cap stayed at 32,768. Pricing is flat within tiers: Mini at $0.7 input and $1.4 output per million tokens, full models at $3 and $6, the older 2.0 and RP 1.0 at $0.8 and $1.6.\n\nFor AI specifically, the useful signal is that capability here is rented, not owned. Every version runs behind an API, which means every inference depends on someone else's datacenter and power contract. The 262,144-token context window is the part that touches infrastructure: long contexts multiply the compute and memory a single request occupies, so the newest models are the most demanding on the serving side even though the price per token did not rise.\n\nWhat the data does not cover is decisive. There are no benchmarks, no parameter counts beyond the 8B label on the oldest model, no knowledge cutoffs for the newer releases, and no hosting or energy details. It cannot say how large these models are, how they were trained, or where they run. It shows a catalog, not a capability.",
